WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.668
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:02.668 --> 00:00:04.960
ASHLEY THOMAS: I'm Ashley
Thomas, a cognitive scientist

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.110
at the McGovern
Institute, at MIT.

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:09.840
I use puppets to
study baby minds

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.080
and how babies make sense
of the world around them.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.180
People used to think that
babies didn't understand

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.910
much at all about the world,
but now, we know that's wrong.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.890
Babies understand a lot.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.900
Even though babies can't
talk, their behavior

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.300
provides clues about
what they're thinking.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.130
Babies look at people
and things they like,

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.630
and they focus their
attention where

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:29.650
they expect things to happen.

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.800
So to figure out what
a baby is thinking,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.600
I measure what they look at.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.250
Here's what I mean.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.750
This is baby Ursula.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:40.080
She is watching Sarah
share food with a puppet.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.240
Now, Ursula sees a
different person, Laura,

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:44.190
passing a ball with the puppet.

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.530
What happens if the
puppet starts crying?

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.400
Who will comfort the sad
puppet, Sarah or Laura?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.640
Ursula can't tell us what she is
thinking, but she can show us.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.470
When Ursula looks
at Sarah first,

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.070
it tells me that she expects
Sarah to comfort the puppet.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.780
These types of
experiments show us

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.640
that babies do understand a lot
about the world around them,

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:07.279
including complex
social relationships.

